questions.prompt:
Which single change makes this loop terminate after printing 1, 2, 3?
int i = 1;
while (i <= 4) {
    System.out.println(i);
    i--;
}

Trace the following program and state its exact output, justifying each pass:
int x = 2;
while (x < 20) {
    System.out.print(x + " ");
    x = x * 2;
}

A student writes the program below intending to print the numbers 1 to 5. Explain what is wrong, and rewrite the program correctly.
int i = 1;
while (i <= 5) {
    System.out.println(i);
}
